it seems neither of the parties are going

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:33.860
to be participating in debates, at least at
least the Republican conference did say that

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.629
they would have won. It's just Trump may not
be participating, but the fact that Biden

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:44.760
doesn't even want to talk to Marianne or Kennedy
seems a little messed up for me.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.420
Speaker 1: Yeah, I mean, listen, I would like
to see debates on both sides. I think Trump

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:55.410
not showing up is pathetic. And I think that
the DNC should organize debates. But I'm also

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:04.089
not naive, obviously. Why? If you are if you
have an incumbent president and you have as

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:09.751
a priority making the incumbent president
president for four more years, why would you

00:01:09.751 --> 00:01:14.400
take the risk? And I know people say, well,
if it were Obama, there would be less risk

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.340
because Obama is better at public speaking
them. But whatever. Why would you create a

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:26.420
situation with the risk that your eventual
nominee ends up hurting themselves with a

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:31.250
bad debate performance? It's sort of like,
obviously, I'm always for debate and more

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:37.240
conversation, but it's also so obvious that
it would be a completely unforced risk for

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:45.649
the DNC to to try to force Biden to debate.
Speaker 2: Right. And given his age and the

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:53.360
fact that he has seemingly more difficulty
to speak. Not that he doesn't get anything

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.070
